@page "/properties"

<SeoHead Title="Style components with typed properties | Quark Suite" Description="Learn Quark variants, Tailwind builders, responsive modifiers, semantic colors, and escape hatches with examples you can read left to right." />

<DocumentationPage Title="Style components with typed properties" Description="Learn Quark variants, Tailwind builders, responsive modifiers, semantic colors, and escape hatches with examples you can read left to right.">

<Section Id="choose-the-api">
    <H2>Start at the right level</H2>
    <UnorderedList><UnorderedListItem><Strong>Component variants:</Strong> use a component's normal choices, such as <Code>ButtonVariant.Outline</Code> and <Code>ButtonSize.Sm</Code>.</UnorderedListItem><UnorderedListItem><Strong>Typed properties:</Strong> use <Code>Padding</Code>, <Code>Gap</Code>, <Code>Width</Code>, <Code>TextColor</Code>, and related builders for individual style concerns.</UnorderedListItem><UnorderedListItem><Strong>Raw styling:</Strong> use <Code>Class</Code>, <Code>Style</Code>, and ordinary HTML attributes for exact CSS or semantics.</UnorderedListItem></UnorderedList>
    <Paragraph>Each component also has behavior-specific parameters. Use its <Anchor Href="components">demo page</Anchor> for the actual API and working examples.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="read-a-chain">
    <H2>Read builder chains left to right</H2>
    <Paragraph><Strong>A modifier configures the next concrete value.</Strong> It does not modify the value before it. A chain can produce several complete Tailwind utilities:</Paragraph>
    <CodeEditor Text="@chain" Language="razor" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
    <Div Class="overflow-x-auto"><Table><Thead>
        <Tr><Th>Expression</Th><Th>Generated classes</Th><Th>Meaning</Th></Tr>
        </Thead>
        <Tbody>
        <Tr><Td><Code>Padding.OnX.Is4.OnY.Is2</Code></Td><Td><Code>px-4 py-2</Code></Td><Td>Horizontal padding 4, vertical padding 2.</Td></Tr>
        <Tr><Td><Code>FlexDirection.Col.OnMd.Row</Code></Td><Td><Code>flex-col md:flex-row</Code></Td><Td>Column layout, switching to a row at medium width.</Td></Tr>
        <Tr><Td><Code>BackgroundColor.Primary.OnHover.Secondary</Code></Td><Td><Code>bg-primary hover:bg-secondary</Code></Td><Td>Primary background with a secondary hover background.</Td></Tr>
        </Tbody>
        </Table>
    </Div>
    <Paragraph>A trailing modifier such as <Code>Padding.Is4.OnX</Code> does not retroactively make the earlier padding horizontal. Write <Code>Padding.OnX.Is4</Code> for that intent.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="responsive-and-state">
    <H2>Responsive and state modifiers use the same rule</H2>
    <CodeEditor Text="@state" Language="razor" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
    <Paragraph>Use <Code>OnMd</Code>, <Code>OnLg</Code>, <Code>OnHover</Code>, <Code>OnFocusVisible</Code>, and other supported modifiers before the value they affect. The modifier APIs are already included through Quark's builders; applications do not need the Modifiers generator just to use them.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="tokens">
    <H2>Named values, arbitrary tokens, and raw classes</H2>
    <Paragraph>Named values keep common cases readable: <Code>Width.IsFull</Code>, <Code>Gap.Is4</Code>, and <Code>Rounded.Lg</Code>. Use <Code>Width.Token("72")</Code> for <Code>w-72</Code> or <Code>MaxWidth.Token("[1400px]")</Code> for an arbitrary width.</Paragraph>
    <Paragraph>Use <Code>Class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"</Code> when a literal Tailwind expression is clearer. Keep the complete class names in source. Runtime interpolation cannot be reliably discovered by a build-time scanner.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="theme-colors">
    <H2>Use semantic colors for reusable UI</H2>
    <Paragraph>Choose <Code>BackgroundColor.Card</Code>, <Code>TextColor.CardForeground</Code>, <Code>BorderColor.Border</Code>, and other semantic tokens. Their values come from the theme, so the same Razor component can work in light and dark mode. <Anchor Href="themes">Set up your application theme</Anchor>.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="composition-and-attributes">
    <H2>Keep the right HTML element</H2>
    <CodeEditor Text="@navigation" Language="razor" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
    <Paragraph><Code>AsChild</Code> lets a component apply its treatment to the child element. Give navigation a real URL; give icon-only actions an accessible label. Pass attributes such as <Code>aria-label</Code>, <Code>data-testid</Code>, and <Code>id</Code> alongside Quark parameters.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="presets">
    <H2>Reuse a styling decision</H2>
    <Paragraph>Quark ships preset tokens such as <Code>QuarkPresets.ContainerWrapper</Code>. A preset applies a set of component properties. Use those built-in tokens directly; the Presets generator is for authoring additional typed registry members from attributed preset classes.</Paragraph>
    <Paragraph>For app-specific repetition, a small Razor component is often the clearest place to keep both the markup and its styling. Use a preset when several different elements should share the same property configuration. <Anchor Href="generators#generator-reference">See the generator roles</Anchor>.</Paragraph>
</Section>

<Section Id="build-output">
    <H2>How a builder becomes CSS</H2>
    <Paragraph><Code>Soenneker.Quark.Gen.Tailwind.Manifest</Code> records complete utilities from builder expressions. <Code>Soenneker.Quark.Gen.Tailwind</Code> then compiles those utilities along with literal classes and the suite manifest. If a utility exists only at runtime, list the permitted classes in your Tailwind input:</Paragraph>
    <CodeEditor Text="@safelist" Language="css" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
    <Paragraph>Rebuild after changing source classes or builders. If the component has the class but no matching CSS, <Anchor Href="troubleshooting#missing-utility">check the manifest and generated stylesheet</Anchor>.</Paragraph>
</Section>

</DocumentationPage>

@code {
    private const string chain = @"<Div Padding=""Padding.OnX.Is4.OnY.Is2""
     FlexDirection=""FlexDirection.Col.OnMd.Row""
     Display=""Display.Flex""
     Gap=""Gap.Is3"">
    Content
</Div>";

    private const string state = @"<Button BackgroundColor=""BackgroundColor.Primary.OnHover.Secondary""
        Variant=""ButtonVariant.Default"">
    Continue
</Button>";

    private const string navigation = @"<Button AsChild=""true"" Variant=""ButtonVariant.Outline"">
    <Anchor Href=""/dashboard"">Open dashboard</Anchor>
</Button>";

    private const string safelist = @"/* tailwind/input.css: enumerate the complete classes you choose at runtime. */
@source inline(""bg-red-500 bg-green-500 md:grid-cols-3"");";
}
